        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="0980" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg886"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Oct. 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1019.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information the copy of a dispatch from the British vice-consul at Harpoot,
                    inclosing formal <pb facs="0981" n="887" xml:id="pg887"/> affidavits, which
                    establish the complicity of the Turkish soldiers in the burning and plundering
                    of the American college in that city.</p>
                <p>This testimony was taken in accordance with my request to the British chargé
                    d’affaires here and furnishes the legation with more convincing evidence of the
                    facts than it possessed before.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>












